Size a released CHARSXP by its length, not by the hash value kept in
its TRUELENGTH.

getVecSizeInVEC() (src/main/memory.c) extends a growable vector to its
TRUELENGTH before ReleaseLargeFreeVectors() subtracts the vector's size
from R_LargeVallocSize.  IS_GROWABLE() tests gp bit 5 and
LENGTH < TRUELENGTH, but for a CHARSXP bit 5 is the "cached" mark, set
on every string, and TRUELENGTH holds the hash value once the string
has been hashed.  A hashed string that is not a symbol's print name
can be collected, and one longer than 128 bytes was then released as
if it were up to 2^28 bytes long.  R_LargeVallocSize wraps below zero,
after which gc() reports about 1.8e19 Vcells in use, R_MAX_VSIZE no
longer limits anything, and vector allocation no longer triggers a
collection.

installNoTrChar() hashes its argument before rejecting a name longer
than 10000 bytes, so unserialize() of a SYMSXP with such a name leaves
exactly that kind of string behind (as does as.name() in R 4.6.1).
Here that defeated the harnesses' vector heap cap (FUZZ_R_MAX_VSIZE):
after a few such inputs garbage was no longer collected and the
process grew until libFuzzer's -rss_limit_mb=2560 killed it.

Found by OSS-Fuzz (libFuzzer_r_unserialize): testcase 4823638474555392,
an unreproducible Out-of-memory with 2.5 GB of 32 MB string vectors
live under the 512Mb cap; 20% of the target's sessions ended that way
on 2026-11-10.  The filed input alone peaks near 545 MB; it reproduces
after 40 inputs that each name a distinct 20000-byte symbol.

Upstream status: R Bugzilla 19195, reported independently on
2026-10-01 with a patch making the same change (unconfirmed);
r-devel/r-svn PR #466, filed 2026-11-10.  The upstream PR also adds a
regression test to tests/reg-fuzz.R, left out here so this carry patch
does not go stale with that file.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

diff --git a/src/main/memory.c b/src/main/memory.c
index b66e983ed2..620b27d86b 100644
--- a/src/main/memory.c
+++ b/src/main/memory.c
@@ -1105,7 +1105,9 @@ static void TryToReleasePages(void)
 /* compute size in VEC units so result will fit in LENGTH field for FREESXPs */
 static R_INLINE R_size_t getVecSizeInVEC(SEXP s)
 {
-    if (IS_GROWABLE(s))
+    /* For a CHARSXP the growable bit is the 'cached' mark and
+       TRUELENGTH may hold a hash value. */
+    if (TYPEOF(s) != CHARSXP && IS_GROWABLE(s))
 	SET_STDVEC_LENGTH(s, XTRUELENGTH(s));
 
     R_size_t size;
